---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import heroImage from "../assets/hero.png";
import AgentPluginSection from "../components/AgentPluginSection.astro";
import ScaleSetSection from "../components/ScaleSetSection.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import goMod from "../../go.mod?raw";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const repoUrl = "https://github.com/actionscommunity/multirunner";
const goVersion = goMod.match(/^go (\S+)/m)?.[1];
const configExample = `provisioning: pool
github:
  scope: repo
  owner: my-user
  repo: my-repo
auth:
  pat: "\${GITHUB_PAT}"
pools:
  - name: linux
    os: linux
    size: 3
    labels: [self-hosted, linux, multirunner-demo]
    docker:
      host: "unix:///var/run/docker.sock"`;
---

<Layout
  title="multirunner | Run GitHub Actions on your own hardware"
  description="Run fresh Linux and Windows GitHub Actions self-hosted runners in parallel on one machine."
>
  <!-- THESIS: One physical host coordinates many clean parallel jobs. This surface refuses the generic developer-tool card grid. -->
  <!-- OWN-WORLD: Cool white, deep ink, cobalt lanes, scarce signal orange, hard rules, flat geometry, and industrial editorial type. -->
  <!-- STORY: Understand the runner model, verify the GitHub-native scaling path, then build or install the operator plugin. -->
  <!-- FIRST VIEWPORT: Copy and actions occupy the left 45 percent; the generated runner chassis owns the right; live commands anchor the bottom. -->
  <!-- FORM: Runner Yard, selected after three visual comps and a rubber-duck prompt review; Azure GPT Image 2 provides the hero and mark. -->

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="page-shell hero-shell">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Run GitHub Actions on your own hardware.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Run Linux and Windows jobs in parallel on hardware you control. Use
          disposable containers or Windows VMs, or opt in to direct execution
          for trusted Windows jobs.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="#get-started">Build from source</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}commands/`}>Read the CLI reference</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <Image
          class="hero-image"
          src={heroImage}
          alt="One hardware host running several parallel blank job modules"
          widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1536]}
          sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 1200px"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="hero-support">
        <div class="terminal-sample" aria-label="Example multirunner commands">
          <code class="shell">multirunner doctor --config config.yaml</code>
          <code class="shell">multirunner run --config config.yaml</code>
        </div>
        <div class="platforms" aria-label="Supported platforms">
          <span>Linux</span>
          <span>Windows</span>
          <span>macOS service host</span>
          <span>Actions scale sets</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="features">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Fast between jobs. Clean for every job.</h2>
        <p>
          A standard self-hosted runner processes one job at a time. multirunner
          provisions ephemeral runner registrations for one job each, up to
          the configured capacity of each pool.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <article>
          <h3>Real parallelism</h3>
          <p>Run multiple runner registrations on one host instead of maintaining each runner by hand.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Ephemeral by default</h3>
          <p>Container and VM runners use a disposable environment. Windows host jobs reuse the host and are not isolated.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Local caches</h3>
          <p>Optionally serve an Actions cache locally and use a Git cache for repository-scoped setups.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Linux and Windows</h3>
          <p>Use a Docker-compatible daemon, Windows containerd with runhcs, or QEMU for Windows VMs.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Pool, autoscale, or scale set</h3>
          <p>Keep runners warm, react to queued work, or let GitHub report desired capacity through Actions runner scale sets.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Host-native service</h3>
          <p>Run under Windows SCM, Linux systemd, or macOS launchd. Enable health and Prometheus endpoints with <code>metrics.listen</code>.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ScaleSetSection />

  <section class="section build-section" id="get-started">
    <div class="page-shell split">
      <div>
        <h2>From source to a three-runner pool.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          In Bash on a Linux host with a running Docker daemon, use Go <code>{goVersion}</code> or later
          and an account that can access the Docker socket. Save the example as
          <code>config.yaml</code> and replace the owner and repository. Supply a
          PAT authorized to administer that repository’s runners.
        </p>
        <p>Prefer a published binary? Choose the OS and architecture at <a href={`${repoUrl}/releases/latest`}>GitHub Releases</a>. Compare the downloaded executable’s SHA-256 with its entry in <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code> (use <code>sha256sum</code> on Linux, <code>shasum -a 256</code> on macOS, or <code>Get-FileHash</code> in PowerShell). Rename it to <code>multirunner</code> (or <code>multirunner.exe</code> on Windows), make it executable on Unix, and put it on your PATH. Check that release’s notes and <code>--help</code>; older binaries may not implement the current source features shown here.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${base}operations/`}>Explore configuration and operations</a>
      </div>
      <div class="code-stack">
        <div>
          <p class="code-label">Build current main</p>
          <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/ActionsCommunity/multirunner.git
cd multirunner
go build ./cmd/multirunner</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="code-label">config.yaml</p>
          <pre data-config-example="pool"><code>{configExample}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="code-label">Validate, then run</p>
          <pre><code>{`read -rsp 'GitHub PAT: ' GITHUB_PAT; echo
export GITHUB_PAT
./multirunner run --config config.yaml --dry-run
./multirunner doctor --config config.yaml
./multirunner run --config config.yaml`}</code></pre>
          <p>Set the workflow’s <code>runs-on</code> to <code>[self-hosted, linux, multirunner-demo]</code>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <AgentPluginSection />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Pick the isolation your jobs need.</h2>
        <p>
          Pools can target separate backends and labels from one configuration.
          Route each workflow job with the same familiar <code>runs-on</code> labels.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="backend-grid">
        <article>
          <p class="backend-kicker">Linux</p>
          <h3>Docker or Podman</h3>
          <p>Use the docker-compatible API with prebuilt minimal, native-build, Node, .NET, Rust, and Go image tiers.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="backend-kicker">Windows host</p>
          <h3>containerd and runhcs</h3>
          <p>Run native Windows containers through the Host Compute Service without requiring Docker Desktop.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="backend-kicker">Linux, Windows, macOS</p>
          <h3>QEMU Windows VMs</h3>
          <p>Boot a Windows golden image with a per-job overlay. See the <a href={`${base}operations/#backends`}>backend guide</a> before selecting host hardware.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section final-section">
    <div class="page-shell final-cta">
      <h2>Make self-hosted runners disposable.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Read the source or build current main with Go.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#get-started">Build from source</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={repoUrl}>Browse the source</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .hero-shell {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: min(820px, calc(100vh - 72px));
  }

  .hero-copy {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    width: 41%;
    padding: var(--space-7) 0 15rem;
  }

  .hero-copy h1 {
    max-width: 9.5ch;
  }

  .hero-copy .lead {
    max-width: 38ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-visual {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 calc((var(--max) - 100vw) / 2);
    z-index: 1;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center;
  }

  .hero-support {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: var(--space-6);
    left: 0;
    z-index: 3;
    width: 43%;
  }

  .terminal-sample {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    color: var(--paper);
    background: var(--ink);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--steel);
    font: 500 clamp(0.7rem, 1.2vw, 0.82rem)/1.6 var(--font-mono);
  }

  .platforms {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  .platforms span {
    padding: 0.28rem 0.52rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--steel);
    font: 600 0.68rem/1.3 var(--font-mono);
  }

  .feature-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .feature-list article {
    min-height: 170px;
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-5) var(--space-5) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .feature-list article:nth-child(odd) {
    padding-right: var(--space-6);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .feature-list article:nth-child(even) {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
  }

  .feature-list p,
  .backend-grid p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--steel);
  }

  .build-section {
    background: var(--cobalt-soft);
  }

  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .split > *,
  .code-stack,
  .code-stack > div {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .split .lead {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .text-link {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .code-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .code-label,
  .backend-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    color: var(--steel);
    font: 600 0.72rem/1.2 var(--font-mono);
  }

  .backend-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .backend-grid article {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .backend-grid article:first-child {
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .backend-grid article:last-child {
    padding-right: 0;
    border-right: 0;
  }

  .final-section {
    background: var(--orange-soft);
  }

  .final-cta {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-left: max(1rem, calc((100vw - var(--max)) / 2));
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .final-cta::after {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    width: clamp(64px, 10vw, 120px);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    background: var(--orange);
    content: "";
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero-shell {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      min-height: auto;
      padding-top: var(--space-7);
    }

    .hero-copy {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .hero-copy h1,
    .hero-copy .lead {
      max-width: none;
    }

    .hero-visual {
      position: relative;
      inset: auto;
      width: calc(100% + 2rem);
      height: 310px;
      margin: var(--space-5) -1rem 0;
    }

    .hero-image {
      width: 150%;
      max-width: none;
      object-position: 80% center;
      transform: translateX(-34%);
    }

    .hero-support {
      position: static;
      width: 100%;
      padding: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-6);
    }

    .feature-list,
    .split,
    .backend-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .feature-list article,
    .feature-list article:nth-child(odd),
    .feature-list article:nth-child(even),
    .backend-grid article,
    .backend-grid article:first-child,
    .backend-grid article:last-child {
      min-height: 0;
      padding: var(--space-4) 0;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .final-cta {
      padding-right: 84px;
    }
  }
</style>
